🗨️Chat Application
📌 Overview

This project is a multi-client network chat application built using Python socket programming.
It follows a client–server architecture over TCP, allowing multiple users to connect to a central chat room and exchange messages in real time.

The application demonstrates core networking concepts such as:

TCP socket communication

Multi-threaded server design

Concurrent client handling

Application-layer communication protocol

✨ Features
🔗 TCP Socket Communication

Ensures reliable and ordered message delivery using the TCP protocol.

👥 Concurrent Clients

The server uses Python's threading module to handle multiple users simultaneously.

💬 Real-time Messaging

Messages sent by any client are broadcast to all other connected clients instantly.

🔔 Join/Leave Notifications

All users receive notifications whenever someone:

joins the chat

leaves the chat

⚙️ Graceful Disconnects

Handles unexpected client disconnections safely and cleans up connections properly.

⭐ Extra Features Implemented
🕒 Message Timestamps

Each message includes a timestamp showing when it was broadcast.

Example:

[14:23:05] Rahul: Hello everyone!
🖥️ Server Logging

The server console logs important events such as:

user connections

user disconnections

messages sent

This helps during debugging and monitoring.

👤 User List Command

Clients can view all active users by typing:

/list
📡 Application-Layer Protocol

All messages are transmitted as UTF-8 encoded plain text strings.

Client → Server Commands
JOIN <username>

Sent immediately after connection to establish identity.

Example:

JOIN Rahul
MSG <message>

Sent whenever a user sends a chat message.

Example:

MSG Hello everyone!
LIST

Requests a list of currently connected users.

QUIT

Gracefully disconnects the client from the server.

Server → Client Responses
📢 Broadcast Messages

Messages sent by users are broadcast to all connected clients.

Example:

[14:23:05] Rahul: Hello everyone!
🔔 System Notifications

Notifications about join/leave events.

Example:

[Server] Rahul has joined the chat.
❗ Error Messages

Sent when a protocol violation occurs.

Example:

Error: Username already exists
🚀 Getting Started
Prerequisites

Make sure you have the following installed:

Python 3.x

No external libraries required

The application only uses Python's built-in libraries:

socket

threading

🖥️ Running the Server

Navigate to the server directory:

cd server

Run the server script:

python server.py

The server will start listening on port:

65432
💻 Running a Client

Open a new terminal window

Navigate to the client directory:

cd client

Run the client script:

python client.py

Enter your username when prompted.

Start chatting!

Useful Client Commands
Show Connected Users
/list
Exit the Chat
/quit
🏗️ Project Design

The application consists of two main modules.

1️⃣ Server (server.py)

Responsibilities:

Listens for incoming client connections

Spawns a new thread for each client

Maintains active users in a global dictionary:

clients = { username : connection }
Server Workflow

Accept client connection

Receive JOIN command

Register the client

Start handle_client thread

Broadcast incoming messages to other users

Thread Safety

Since multiple threads modify shared resources, a thread lock is used to prevent race conditions:

threading.Lock()
2️⃣ Client (client.py)

Responsibilities:

Connect to the server

Handle user input

Display incoming messages

Client Thread Model

The client uses two threads:

Main Thread

Waits for user input (stdin)

Sends messages to the server

Receiver Thread

Continuously listens for messages from the server

Prints them to the terminal

This ensures asynchronous communication, allowing users to receive messages while typing.

